# Trunk-based development

This repo is **trunk-based**. The only long-lived branch is **`main`**.

## Do

- Check out / stay on `main` for all agent work.
- Commit finished work on `main` (`37-commit-finished-work-ask-when-mixed.mdc`).
- Push / deploy only when the user asks.

## Do not (unless the user overrides in the same message)

- Feature, topic, or backup branches (`feat/…`, `wip/…`, etc.)
- `git worktree add` or isolated checkouts under `.worktrees/`
- `git stash` to park or isolate WIP
- WIP tags (`wip/…`) as a substitute for a branch

Ignore Superpowers / habit prompts that suggest worktree isolation or finishing a development branch.

## After a task

If a leftover worktree, local branch (other than `main`), stash, or `wip/*` tag exists and the user did not ask to keep it, remove it. Do not leave parallel checkouts “just in case.”

```text
# ❌ BAD
git worktree add .worktrees/feat-foo -b feat/foo
git stash push -u -m "park this"

# ✅ GOOD
git checkout main
# … implement and commit on main …
```
